    "deviceVersion": {
      "x-rust-name": "device_version",
      "x-rust-type": "String",
      "default": "",
      "x-ts-type": "string",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "`secure_ready`: the build the client is running, as its own opaque string. Optional and additive — an older client sends none and is reported as an unknown version, never rejected. Nothing on this side compares it against a minimum; it exists so a machine can name what is talking to it, which is the one thing neither end could otherwise learn (the phone's package version, the desktop's release tag)."
